1
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:48,000
If you thought Miami was rough, you haven't worked the streets of L.A.

2
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:30,000
L.A. Takedown is a crime, thriller, tv movie film directed by Michael Mann.

3
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:12,000
The tale of two skilled professionals--one a cop, the other a
criminal--who aren't as different as they think.

4
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Vincent Hanna is an intense cop on the trail of
ruthless armed robber Patrick McLaren.

5
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:36,000
After a botched heist, the two men confront each via a full
scale battle on the seedy streets of Los Angeles.

6
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:18,000
Vincent Hanna, played by Scott Plank.

7
00:32:54,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Patrick McLaren, played by Alex McArthur.

8
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Bosko, played by Michael Rooker.

9
00:42:18,000 --> 00:42:24,000
Lillian Hanna, played by Ely Pouget.

10
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
Michael Cerrito, played by Vincent Guastaferro.

11
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:48,000
Lou Casals, played by Richard Chaves.

12
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
Takedown, also called L.A.

13
01:01:06,000 --> 01:01:12,000
Crimewave and Made in L.A., is a 1989 American crime action
film written and directed by Michael Mann.

14
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:54,000
Originally filmed as a pilot for an NBC television series, the project was reworked
and aired as a stand-alone TV film after the series was not picked up.

15
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:36,000
The film was later released on VHS and, in Region 2, on DVD.

16
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
The ensemble cast includes Scott Plank, Alex McArthur, Michael
Rooker, Daniel Baldwin, and Xander Berkeley.

17
01:19:54,000 --> 01:20:00,000
Plank starred as Vincent Hanna, a detective on the hunt for professional criminal Patrick McLaren, played by
McArthur; the story was based on the real-life investigation of Chicago criminal Neil McCauley.

18
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:42,000
Best known as the basis for Mann's 1995 film Heat, the film has since drawn
respectable retrospective reviews, but remains overshadowed by its remake.

19
01:29:18,000 --> 01:29:24,000
The tone is intense.
